id: pm-slack-npwn
title: Bound lifecycle notification bursts with complete coalescing receipts
description: "Coalesce queued delivery events using the durable Slack outbox, separately from tracker-state digest and periodic standup reports."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-slack#151"
created_at: "2026-10-24T07:17:48.932Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T21:48:08.822Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T21:48:08.810Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T21:48:08.810Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Order permutations yield stable summaries; Urgent events bypass the batch; Every suppressed event appears in an omission or coalescing receipt
resolution: "Deterministic coalescing bounds bursts, lets urgent blockers bypass limits and accounts for every suppressed event in receipts."
expected_result: Order permutations yield stable summaries; Urgent events bypass the batch; Every suppressed event appears in an omission or coalescing receipt
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/151, merged 2026-10-24T09:51:25Z, merge 22248b97ca6d89f2f750fb596a84c4c418b52572: Deterministic coalescing bounds bursts, lets urgent blockers bypass limits and accounts for every suppressed event in receipts."
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T07:17:59.856Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: pinned pm SDK exposes lifecycle history verification/replay and complete tracker reads, but no delivery coalescer. Existing slack digest summarizes current tracker state; pm-slack-standup produces periodic project reports and snapshot trends. This feature groups queued outbox lifecycle deliveries by item, destination and fixed time window. Reuse verified SDK history capture and durable delivery/reconciliation, with a pure typed planner, bounded CLI receipts and urgent-blocker bypass. No git dependency, tracker mutation or remote posting in preview."
  "2026-10-24T07:27:36.966Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses a pure deterministic planner and the existing durable outbox. SDK verified history captures timestamp and priority per committed transition. Same-item/destination/fixed-window summaries retain source receipts; priority 0/1 and every blocker bypass routine bounds. Claims and group reconciliation fence concurrent senders and uncertain delivery. Public-data validation at main 0e4c89e: 87 items, 87 verified streams, 658 history entries, 222 lifecycle events; budget 5 produced 86 notifications (81 urgent plus 5 routine summaries covering 8 events), 133 deferred, zero waiting, 222 receipts, max summary 58 characters. Three order variants equal, zero-budget urgent-only, all exported tracker bytes unchanged. Priority 0 discovered in public data is supported as urgent. CLI source overlap rechecked at 06eff3bf1 and standup at f584c70; only CLI flag-list coalescing exists, unrelated to delivery."
  "2026-10-24T07:34:39.388Z",codex-agent,"Validation: linked targeted command passed 111 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations; typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint passed. Native Bun acceptance passed through the compiled entry: one recovered lifecycle plus two coalesced events, two acknowledged HTTP sends and zero duplicates in a no-git tracker. Planner targeted coverage is 100 percent lines, branches and functions. Behavioral revert proof: disabling grouping, disabling urgent classification, and truncating member receipts each made the relevant targeted test fail (one test, zero passes, one failure), restoring the exact source after each run. Additional SQLite trigger regression verifies that event-context refusal rolls back the intent and claim refusal rolls back all members before HTTP. Full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI because the host is saturated; thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T07:37:56.984Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/151 . Source head 6c3c11c22c5b6963dce27859238c60e4109634c5 passed CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40074736357 : Node 22 and 26 each passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check, 318 tests per gate, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 100 percent lines/branches/functions over all three source files. Both native Bun acceptance jobs passed (one recovered lifecycle plus two coalesced events, two acknowledged HTTP sends, zero duplicates). CodeQL passed. Automated review evidence is missing: Greptile trial ended, Sourcery budget exhausted, CodeRabbit auto-review skipped by repository eligibility, Cubic neutral. No review approval is claimed. Scope complete for orchestrator review; item stays in progress and will be released, never closed. Final metadata-only head will rerun CI and the PR body will record that exact-head run. No pm CLI or SDK defect encountered."
  "2026-10-24T09:30:42.724Z",codex-agent,"Review round: retry cleanup releases members before removing group mappings. Audit covers claim, group, send completion, typed and transport failure, retry, crash recovery and reconciliation. Plan: SQLite critical sections plus unique attempt ownership; cleanup deletes only its own mappings and releases members last. Exercise two drainers on one non-git tracker at every SQL boundary, fault rollback and stale sender completion. Merge current main first; pinned host health currently reports an inherited pm-github host-version mismatch."
  "2026-10-24T09:36:02.528Z",codex-agent,"Implemented SQLite transaction fencing for plain/group claims, attempt completion and reconciliation. Unique attempt tokens are separate from deterministic planner IDs. Retry cleanup deletes mappings only by its token, then releases members last. Forced reconciliation retires the old token, so late senders cannot overwrite or delete a newer claim. Audit documented in docs/coalescing-validation.md. Boundary suite: 156 passed, zero failures; real process death, ABORT/ROLLBACK faults and stale plain/group completions included. Native Bun acceptance extended for retry cleanup and late completion. Local lint is the configured docstring gate plus git diff --check; no separate lint script exists."
  "2026-10-24T09:37:41.244Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: kept every regression test unchanged and reverted only outbox.ts to its pre-fix merge-parent version. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"retry and failure cleanup\" test/outbox-interleaving.test.ts exited nonzero, reproducing orphan ambiguity after sibling reconciliation; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"stale grouped and plain\" test/outbox-interleaving.test.ts also exited nonzero because late old completions overwrite the newer group. Tests import source directly, so compiled output is not involved. Restored the exact fixed source bytes before continuing. Full coverage with the fix: 474 passed, zero failed/skipped/cancelled; 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all three source files. Boundary suite alone: 156 passed."
  "2026-10-24T09:38:42.323Z",codex-agent,"Revert counts (including parent tests): retry/failure boundary proof 9 tests, 6 passed, 3 failed (retry and typed-retry both lose whole-group recovery); stale completion proof 9 tests, 0 passed, 9 failed (all eight grouped/plain outcome cases fail). Restored fix then pm test pm-slack-npwn --run --progress passed all three linked commands: existing targeted suite 111 passed, native Bun acceptance passed, extended targeted suite 201 passed; zero failures/skips/cancellations. Local runtime-only health used an isolated home to exclude unrelated global extension skew; pinned pm merge install regenerated the tracked merge fence. No history rewrite or SDK bump."
  "2026-10-24T09:40:52.761Z",codex-agent,"Local full gates passed with isolated HOME and git configuration: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each ran 474 tests, all passed with zero failures/skips/cancellations, and measured 100 percent lines/branches/functions across coalescing.ts, index.ts and outbox.ts. Typecheck, build, docstring lint, production audit, pack dry run, changelog check and release workflow verifiers passed. Native Bun acceptance and isolated pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passed. Pushing the review fix for CI Node 22/26 npm+Bun full-gate evidence; tracker stays in progress pending orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-24T09:43:20.845Z",codex-agent,"CI verified source head 8de68c9ec76cfa7cc3c9f4d99d2c0ed46d945633: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40082931607 . Node 22 and 26 each passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check: 474 tests per gate, zero failures/skips/cancellations (four gates, 1896 test executions), 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all three source files. Both native Bun acceptance jobs passed with zero duplicates, including retry cleanup and stale completion preserving the peer group. Tracker health and committed output checks passed in both jobs. All claim/group/send/retry/failure/crash/reconcile transitions audited; SQL boundary regression and process-death/fault matrix recover whole groups. Main rechecked unchanged. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; item stays in progress, never closed. No new pm CLI/SDK defect encountered. Slack response loss still requires explicit reconciliation; force retry still requires operator verification of sender absence."
